// aug24a class G (campaign witness, hz0): COMPILE-MODE SKEW again, a
// different mechanism from fusion-mutates-tvars-aug2026 and this one IS
// oracle-visible — both modes reject, with DIFFERENT text:
//
//   graphix --check            .. type mismatch List<'a: unbound> does not contain `Cons(bool, bool)
//   graphix --no-fusion --check .. type mismatch List<'a: bool>    does not contain `Cons(bool, bool)
//
// `Env::seed_typedef_refs` — the eager pass that fills every typedef's
// carried resolution cells — ran inside `if ctx.fusion.enabled`, so the
// STDLIB compiled with filled cells in the default mode and empty ones
// under `--no-fusion`. A ref whose cell is filled and one whose cell is
// empty take different paths through `contains` (`ref_id` keys identity
// off the cell; `lookup_ref` resolves through it), so the failed
// unification against `List<'a>` binds the call site's `'a` in one mode
// and not the other. The verdict agreed; the inference channel did not,
// which is the part that could have differed on a program that COMPILES.
// A user-local typedef with the same shape always agreed — the skew
// needed a typedef compiled in an earlier `compile()` call.
//
// Fixed by seeding in both modes (the pass is a typecheck-time fact, not
// a fusion one): `seed_typedef_refs()` moved above the fusion gate.
list::drop(i64:0, `Cons(true, true))
